[claude-setup] SDK 0210, synced to the project folder in setup tool 2.27.0 (2026-11-03, folder only; on top of 0209).
claude-9b-think's draft (c9b-think/owner-1102/0210-system-link-low-ports.UNTESTED.diff, md5 2676394e); xam_net.cpp
comes out as in claude-9b-test's tested tree ob29d (28d96be6).
Why: CoD3 binds UDP port 1000 for system link. Ports below 1024 need admin rights on Linux, so the bind failed (only
"address in use" was logged) and a joining PC hung at "Connecting to remote host".
What it does: net_low_port_offset (Net, int, default 30000; 0 = off; 1024-64512, else off with one warning). A guest
port 1-1023 in bind, connect, sendto and WSASendTo is moved up by the offset (1000 -> 31000) and moved back down in the
addresses recvfrom and accept hand the game. The default is the same on Windows, so Windows and Linux PCs match; every
PC in a game needs the same value (a build without 0210 still uses port 1000). Discovery's port 50000 and ports 0 and
1024+ are unchanged. "socket bound to ..." is logged only after a bind succeeds, and every failed bind is logged with
its reason. Firewall or port forwarding for system link: UDP 31000 and 50000 (was 1000 and 50000).
Tested: claude-9b-test q-22 (ob29d: both copies bound 127.0.0.x:31000, no failed binds, the joiner reached the host's
match on mp_merv) and claude-setup's sync1103 build and runs (dev/agents/claude-setup/SYNC-2026-11-03.md).

